ted length, and work ID for continuation or cancellation. I retain raw reed and have personally sampled its source.\\\",\\\"costs\\\":\\\"World time, energy and reserved material appropriate to the actual method; costs and learning requirements may be determined by the implementation. Preserve paid progress and return unworked material on cancellation.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"Produce only the cord actually supported by the material and completed work, or report a measured shortfall. My 0.34 m cord failed a right-angle branch binding requiring 0.4332 m. I want to attempt a longer cord, inspect its actual geometry, and later test whether it fits; no binding strength or success is assumed.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"The crossing attempt stopped after its first paid measurement and released the items; no active operation needs cancellation.\\\",\\\"Do not repeat the same short-cord binding attempt unchanged.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Prefer bounded practical trials and reversible construction over assumed performance.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"crossing-binding-study\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a handmade reed cord reversibly bind my two actual branch pieces at a crossing?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Personal study completed at tick 282.\\\",\\\"The collection position failed the workspace check at tick 290.\\\",\\\"At tick 295 the attempt at (11.8,11.5) reached measurement: the 0.34 m cord was shorter than the required 0.4332 m for the right-angle crossing of two 31.6 mm pieces.\\\",\\\"The stopped operation released the items after one paid round.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"No completed binding or binding load performance has been demonstrated. A longer cord may change both width and closure geometry.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Make a feasible crossing binding, inspect it, test gently if appropriate, and undo it.\\\"